 "capsule": "From Oleg's capture of Kiev in 882 until the Mongol destruction of the city in 1240, Kievan Rus' bound the East Slavic lands into a federation of principalities under the Rurikid princes of Kiev, converted to Orthodox Christianity by Grand Prince Vladimir I around 988. It reached its height under Yaroslav the Wise (1019-1054), whose law code (Russkaya Pravda), dynastic marriages, and patronage of Kiev's Cathedral of St. Sophia marked a golden age of Rus' culture, before the Lyubech Congress of 1097 formalized a rotating princely succession that increasingly fragmented the realm into rival appanages. Weakened by that fragmentation, Kievan Rus' was overrun by the Mongols, with Kiev sacked by Batu Khan's forces in December 1240.",
